  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is raining.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ It is not winter.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\u00acA\u21d2\u00acB.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $\u00acA:$ It is not raining.\n\n- $\u00acB:$ It is winter.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If it is not raining, then it is winter.",
